Looking at the demos, I see a pattern: multi-cell "boundary" runs (which stay unchanged) and single "source" cells (which become 4 and fill columns/rows toward the boundary runs with the source's color). In demo 2 (horizontal runs at top and bottom like the test), the top run filled its columns downward to the bottom run's row, and each source filled its column downward to just before the bottom run.

Applying to the test: 9-runs at top (cols 6-7) and bottom (cols 0-1) are boundaries; the single 2s at (3,0) and (12,1) are sources that fill downward toward the bottom run, turning into 4; the top run's columns 6-7 fill down to row 28.

